Differing from the Apache License 2.0 only in the following respects.  Where
Part A and Part B conflict, Part A governs.

A.1  COMMERCIAL USE IS PERMITTED, SUBJECT TO THREE CONDITIONS

Commercial use of this software is allowed without a separate agreement —
including using it inside a company, shipping it as a component of another
product, modifying the source, and charging for work that incorporates it.
The following three conditions are the exceptions.

  (a) No white-labelling.
      If you distribute the software, or a derivative work of it, to end users,
      you may not remove, replace, or obscure the product name, application
      icon, or copyright notices that the software displays to the user.  You
      may add your own notices alongside them, and you may state that your
      product is based on this project.

      What this does NOT restrict: modifying the source for your own internal
      use; distributing a modified version to other developers; naming your
      fork something else in your source repository.  This condition is about
      what the end user sees, not about what you call your checkout.

  (b) No multi-tenant hosting.
      Unless authorized in writing, you may not operate this software, or a
      derivative work of it, as a service that drives, controls, or reads
      devices belonging to third parties (a "multi-tenant environment").
      One operator running the software on its own devices, or on devices it is
      responsible for, is not a multi-tenant environment and is permitted.

  (c) This file must travel with the software.
      Redistributions must include a copy of this license, and modified
      versions must carry prominent notices stating that you changed the files
      (this is Apache 2.0 §4(b), restated here because it is the condition most
      often dropped).

A.2  CONTRIBUTIONS

By submitting a contribution to this project, you agree that:

  (a) You license your contribution to KUAFUAI and to every recipient
      of the software under this same license (Apache 2.0 as modified here);
      and

  (b) You additionally grant KUAFUAI a perpetual, worldwide,
      royalty-free, irrevocable copyright license to use, reproduce, modify,
      distribute, and sublicense your contribution under other license terms.
      This is what allows the project to be offered commercially in parallel
      with this open-source license, and it is why the grant is broader than
      (a).

  You retain copyright to your contribution.  If you are contributing on behalf
  of an employer, you confirm you have permission to do so.

  You represent that you are legally entitled to grant the above and that your
  contribution is your original work, or that you have identified its source and
  any applicable third-party license in your submission.

A.3  TRADEMARKS

Apache 2.0 §6 already withholds any trademark license, and this project relies
on that: no right is granted to use the project's name, logo, or product
identity except as required for reasonable and customary use in describing the
origin of the software.  Forking the code does not grant the right to present
your fork as an official release.

